 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? It' not random, it's just not the order you' used to. In German, the noun comes after the office title, not the other way around. Yes, it is. So instead of saying, Ich bin die Beraterin für Unterschiede zwischen Aktiengesetz und Bürgerliches Gesetz, you'd say, Ich bin die Beraterin für Unterschiede zwischen Aktiengesetz und Bürgerliches Gesetz. It's not absurd, it' how German works. You just need to retrain your brain a little. Most people do. The order feels wrong at first, but that's just because you' used the other way. It's bit of both. Me too. Which one do you want to try first, red for active voice, or green for passive voice?",
